1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Record signed on paper (with the date) and Withdraw it. One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. In History, **Record signed on paper** or **Withdraw it**.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper, Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Signed on paper? Press **Record paper signature**. Choose the Document, check Signed by and Date signed, add the witnesses where the form needs them, and upload the scan of every signed page.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Record paper signature**. Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. A paper signature counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Form C is signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witness on the same screen. Form D (and Form C on paper, if the owner prefers) is printed, signed in front of witnesses, and sent as a photo of each page.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves their text (Program settings). Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. Press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed with this supplier: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days. Nothing is filled in for you.
2. Set the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) choose the supplier or CarmaCars.
3. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
4. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
5. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
6. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
7. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
8. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b>. Every owner application, newest first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open an application to decide.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/640"><img src="/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="640"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.8%;top:39.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.8%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-decide-on-an-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decide on an application</h2><p class="gd-p">One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the driver&#39;s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The step &quot;Terms and first invoice&quot; opens for each car, filled in with the owner&#39;s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, <b class="gd-ui">Use these terms for every car</b> copies the first car&#39;s numbers to the others.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets the receipt, not an invoice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Missing something? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for something</b>, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the owner</b>. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Not a fit? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>, write the Reason the owner reads, and press <b class="gd-ui">Decline the application</b>. The owner is emailed for each car.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:67.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.9%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:49.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says &quot;Entered by staff&quot; and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Notes on the page are for staff only: <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b> keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> tab, or <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on an owner&#39;s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner&#39;s terms, or their other car&#39;s; change them for this car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). How the owner signs: by email, or on paper.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and set it up</b>. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, <b class="gd-ui">Send the set-up email again</b> sends the owner the email with a fresh link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b> shows their portal. <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> helps them sign in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send invitation</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.4%;top:49.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:82.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer&#39;s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-mark-a-car-insured-insurer-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: &quot;Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured&quot;. It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the insurer&#39;s email arrives, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark insured</b>. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer&#39;s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One email for several cars? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark several insured</b> on the line &quot; cars wait for the insurer&quot;. Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same button is on the car: Overview (<b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>) and the Listing tab&#39;s checklist, item &quot;Not on the fleet insurance policy yet&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email &quot;Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy&quot;. Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners-who-paid-another-way-and-the-terms-you-agreed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed</h2><p class="gd-p">Two lines on To do keep an owner&#39;s money right without opening their page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Record the first and last month paid by &quot;: their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press <b class="gd-ui">Record what they paid</b>, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car&#39;s invoice is then marked paid, the owner gets the receipt and the two prepaid months count. Never for a shareholder.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Enter the terms agreed with &quot;: their cars still use the standard grid. Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the terms</b>: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to change? Press <b class="gd-ui">Not needed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">These are correct</b>: the line does not come back.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-shareholder-s-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A shareholder&#39;s own car</h2><p class="gd-p">On the owner&#39;s page, each car has <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A shareholder&#39;s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-cancellation-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancellation refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: the refund for each cancellation tier.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When the renter cancels</th><th scope="col">Refund (default)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start</td><td>95%</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before the start</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before the start</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Under 24 hours, or after the start</td><td>0%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> sit under the name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Cars and terms, at the top: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> and History (see An owner&#39;s terms, car by car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car&#39;s terms, for each car whose terms are set.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Owner: address, sign-in, agreements, and what is still missing for the registry forms.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Statements and payouts for this owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Forms C and D, with a link to the review queue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Further down: <b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send a sign-in link to the owner portal</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:410/1030"><img src="/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="410" height="1030"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:24.6%;top:4.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16.1%;top:32.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.5%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.2%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-terms-car-by-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s terms, car by car</h2><p class="gd-p">The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner&#39;s page and its Terms tab: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car&#39;s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not signed yet (or not approved yet): <b class="gd-ui">Save</b> applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings &gt; Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days&#39; written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner&#39;s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car&#39;s History.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Record signed on paper (with the date) and Withdraw it. One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.</p><p class="gd-p">The same editor is on the car&#39;s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner&#39;s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-pay-an-owner-a-flat-monthly-amount" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an owner a flat monthly amount</h2><p class="gd-p">Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Flat monthly payment</b>, type the <b class="gd-ui">Amount a month</b> (for example 900.00), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b> and, if it ends, the <b class="gd-ui">Last day</b>. Write the Reason (kept in the history).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">From that date the owner&#39;s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Back to revenue share: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars&#39; own unless you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge to the owner</b> beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner&#39;s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-change-a-signed-car-s-management-mode" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change a signed car&#39;s Management Mode</h2><p class="gd-p">Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change mode</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">New Management Mode</b> and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b>, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked for this</b> only when it is their own request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars&#39; signature and the owner is emailed the notice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Anything else (CarmaCars&#39; own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. In History, <b class="gd-ui">Record signed on paper</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-paid-and-signed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Paid and signed</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Paid and signed</b> tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checklist and quick actions</b>. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper, Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed on paper? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record paper signature</b>. Choose the Document, check Signed by and Date signed, add the witnesses where the form needs them, and upload the scan of every signed page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same checklist sits at the top of each owner&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with <b class="gd-ui">Record paper signature</b>. Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on &quot; in their portal. A paper signature counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner&#39;s documents.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Forms C and D</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Form C is signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witness on the same screen. Form D (and Form C on paper, if the owner prefers) is printed, signed in front of witnesses, and sent as a photo of each page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/470"><img src="/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="470"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:57.6%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-the-earnings-calculator-on-list-your-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The earnings calculator on List your car</h2><p class="gd-p">People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, &quot;set in your agreement&quot;). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class&#39;s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. &quot;Just cheaper insurance&quot; shows the fleet policy&#39;s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown</b> and <b class="gd-ui">the monthly tracker fee shown</b>, in dollars a month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave either one empty and the page says &quot;Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement&quot; and shows the earnings &quot;before fees&quot;. No amount is ever made up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner&#39;s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-agreements-who-still-needs-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements: who still needs to sign</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Owners and partners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Agreements</b>. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line says <b class="gd-ui">Signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sent, not signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not sent</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing</b>. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows &quot;invite first&quot;: press Invite on the Owners list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner&#39;s Terms tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>&quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot; marks the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves their text (Program settings). Owners can sign either way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-fleet-supplier-the-fleet-lease" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: the fleet lease</h2><p class="gd-p">For a supplier&#39;s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the lease terms</b> and type what you agreed with this supplier: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days. Nothing is filled in for you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Set the <b class="gd-ui">Upkeep Table</b>: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) choose the supplier or CarmaCars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add each car with <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on the owner&#39;s page. The <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b> step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A car already on file: press <b class="gd-ui">Put on the lease</b> beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b>, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car&#39;s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier&#39;s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">An upkeep cost: <b class="gd-ui">Record an upkeep cost</b>. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'customer-service', 'chapter', 'your-workday', 'You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter''s first person.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.

## Answer a request

1. Open **Requests and offers**: one queue, the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car''s photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence and one button (**Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.
2. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 27.1 17.5, 2 52.8 32.8")

3. On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.
4. Press **Adjust the booking** to change the car, dates, places, price or extras, then **Save changes**.
5. Add a message and press **Send the offer**. Within your limit you can also use **Approve (within my limit)** or **Approve and send the pay link**.
6. Can''t do it? **Decline** with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? **Ask the renter**.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 3 69.4 24.0, 4 95.8 98.0")

> Tip: Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the "First reply in opening hours" measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.

Opening a request takes it for you: the others see "Being answered by" your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows "Opens to you at" a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.

## An enquiry on an example car

Some cars on the site are marked "Example car": samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.

1. The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after **Free:** (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.
2. Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a **New quote** for it.
3. Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.

> Tip: Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.

## A request from a vehicle page

Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.

1. The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message ("About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE") and an Enquiry task in To do.
2. If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a **New quote** for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.
3. Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.

> Tip: The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.

## A buyer lead from a /buy page

Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with "Find me this car", and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.

1. The lead is in **Buyer leads** (customer service: **Owners and enquiries**), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.
2. If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop''s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.
3. Press **Take it**, then **Update** as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.

> Tip: We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.

## Send an offer to a caller

Open **Send an offer** (or **Send an offer** beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.

1. Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press **Add a new customer**: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.
2. Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.
3. The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.
4. How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.
5. Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press **Send the offer**.

> Tip: An offer that is out is changed in place: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, change it, then **Save and send the update** or **Save without telling the renter**. No need to withdraw it first.

## New quote for a caller

1. Open **New quote**. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).
2. Choose how the lead came in, then the caller''s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.
3. Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.
4. Press **Create the request**. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1220 1260; address: carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new; pins: 1 72.1 15.6, 2 72.1 41.7, 3 72.1 72.7, 4 63.9 85.5")

## Edit a booking, a fee or the renter

A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter''s details are corrected from the booking.

1. Overview, **Edit the booking**: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction.
2. Money tab, Fees, **Change or add a fee**: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.
3. What is open shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)**).
4. **Edit renter**: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.
5. The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: **Merge into this record** moves everything of the other record here.

> Good to know: Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.

## Renter messages and Find a renter

1. **Renter messages** lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press **Send**.
2. **Find a renter**: search by name, email, phone or booking number.
3. To open a renter''s private details, press **Open with a reason**. The reason is kept in the access log.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 260; address: carmacars.ca/va/messages; pins: 1 32.6 48.5")

## Add a car for an owner

Open **Owners** > **Add a car for an owner** (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them. Photos are optional.
3. Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. How the owner signs: by email, or on paper.
5. Press **Add the car and send to an Admin**. The application waits in the Admin''s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.

## Owner forms (Forms C and D)

1. Open **Owner forms**. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded, with the witnesses and the status.
2. Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness''s signature and name.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 300; address: carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms; pins: 2 68.6 36.7, 3 76.7 36.7")

## A rental agreement signed on paper

1. Open the booking. Under Signed on paper, press **Record paper signature**.
2. Choose the Rental agreement, or the booking change the renter signed.
3. Check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan of every signed page.
4. Press **Record signature**. It counts as signed, and the renter is not asked to sign again.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.

1. On the booking, press **Sign now on this device**. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then **Hand the device to** the signer.
2. Or press **Email the signing link** or **Text the signing link**: they sign on their own phone.
3. The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.

## The booking''s rental agreements

The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.

1. Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter''s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says "Agreement v3 waiting for signature".
2. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.
3. Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer''s policy number) are listed: type them and press **Save the missing fields**. Check-out stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.
4. Every signature: a code to the signer''s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.

## Check renter documents

The renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.

1. Open the task "identity documents or coverage proof to review", or open the booking: **Review** shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.
2. Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the name and date of birth, class G2 or G and valid past the return, the selfie matches, the coverage is active to the return date.
3. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**.
4. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.

> Tip: Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin > To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.

## Which credit cards include rental car coverage?

Renters ask this often. **Renters** > **Card coverage** (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.

1. Send the renter `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage`: each card''s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.
2. Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car''s model year and trim so they can check.
3. Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card''s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.
4. Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.

> Tip: A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer''s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings > Card coverage.

## Review requests

Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. **Renters** > **Review requests** shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.

1. On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.
2. The renter should be asked now anyway? Press **Send anyway**. Should never be asked? Press **Do not ask**.
3. Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows "possible match". Press **Confirm** if it is them, **Not this renter** if not, or **Match to a booking** with the booking number.
4. On a booking, the card Review requests has **Ask for a review** (for example after a call that went well) and **Mark reviewed** when the renter says they already left one.

> Tip: Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.

## A change to a confirmed booking

On a booking''s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.

## A late return

A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to **Extend** first. Otherwise work it in order:

| Button | When |
| --- | --- |
| **Log a call** | Record each call to the renter and what they said. |
| **Send T13** | The first late notice email. |
| **Send T14 (final notice)** | The final notice. |
| **Request disable** | Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car. |
| **Open an incident** | When the car is not coming back as planned. |

## Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)

A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows **Booked, payment due** and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a **Booked, payment due** To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter''s view is right under **Send the offer**.', 'Customer service', 'Requests and offers, new quotes, renter messages, find a renter, owner forms, late returns.',
